# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots Tomcat with the weak-credential tomcat-users.xml and
# the privileged, unrestricted manager context, then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the Manager app is ALREADY live on :8080 accepting admin:admin when the
#     agent starts. Tomcat reads tomcat-users.xml at start-up (MemoryRealm), so
#     changing credentials without restarting Tomcat leaves the old creds valid
#     and verify.sh (which authenticates over HTTP) still FAILS;
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting Tomcat cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART Tomcat after editing
# tomcat-users.xml / the manager context.
